kUserQuestion` frame (no live claude). Added `gate_adapter.py` to parse stream-json into a prompt-box record (`question, options, tool_use_id, header, multiSelect`), with `mark_awaiting_input` persisting `state=awaiting-input`.\n\n- **Wave 6 (Lane wiring + concurrency) â€” GO, 0 fix iters:** Added `lanes.py` with the frozen lane map (researchâ†’researchPrime / planâ†’Crucible / buildâ†’Foreman â†’ {skill, prompt-seed, output subdir, gate flag}); `launch_lane()` resolves the project, scaffolds the per-project output dir, passes it to the engine via `--skill/--output-dir/--prompt-seed`, and writes a `launch.pointer.json` as on-disk proof. `job_runner.py` gained a concurrency layer: `_ACTIVE_LANE` keyed `(project_id, lane)` (same-lane serialized, cross-lane concurrent) and `_FOLDER_BUILD` keyed `folder_path`.\n\n- **Wave 7 (Versioned history + report viewer + cost rollup + auto-commit) â€” GO after 1 fix iter:** Added `effort_history.py` (job-id-scoped append-only pointer-records under `.anchor/projects/<id>/<lane>/efforts/`, index reversed on read so newest = index 0, nothing deleted on re-run, cost capture from the result envelope, per-effortâ†’laneâ†’project rollups, scoped per-effort `git -C <folder>` auto-commit with no push) and `report_viewer.py` (PDF-by-default else stdlib mdâ†’HTML Reader, traversal-safe). Vendored REAL KaTeX 0.16.11 under `vendor/katex/`.\n\n- **Wave 8 (Shareable, data-free distribution) â€” GO after 1 fix iter:** Added `distro.py` (deny-by-default manifest staging + no-personal-data scan), `dist_manifest.txt`, planted-secret fixtures, and `test_distro_scan`. Initial review was BOTH NO-GO â€” BLOCKER-1: `distro.py` hard-coded the real email and would ship it (PII leak passing only via self-suppression); MAJOR-1: the `distro-scan: allow` marker was globally exploitable; MAJOR-2: the token scan missed unquoted secrets. These were fixed in the iteration (gate had reached GREEN 117 passed before the refute pass forced the fixes).\n\n- **Wave 9 (Deliverables + taskâ†”project activation, TERMINAL) â€” GO, 0 fix iters:** Added `deliverables.py` with per-type success contracts (doc = exists+nonempty via `report_viewer`; script/skill = exit 0 AND result-no-error via `is_error` envelope; program = exit 0 within timeout), enforcing stdin=DEVNULL, non-interactive execution, timeout, and tree-kill reap (no orphans). `anchor_gui.py` gained the project-tasks view (filtered by parsed `Project:` field), deliverables render, and token-gated `/api/rnd/link_task` & `/api/rnd/run_deliverable`; `anchor.py` gained the `link_task`/`link` CLI.\n\n- **Overall:** This build trio (rnd-v1) shipped Waves 2â€“9 of the Anchor R&D control surface in one execution log â€” all waves reached GO, four cleanly (Waves 4, 6, 9) and the rest after a single fix iteration, with Wave 8 surfacing and then closing real PII/secret-scan blockers via the adversarial review."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":72354,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8c4db46-b304-42a2-8842-2f950b5217f4","uuid":"4fd8d2ee-6af8-4e5e-9641-78831c4b8c91","request_id":"req_011Cc9RuNjwM8XpPJUGbqX16"}
